From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:37:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] renderer: drop alpha tests that every fragment passes

Infected keeps the GE's alpha test (greater than 0) on for nearly every draw, so nearly every program had a discard.
When a draw's fragments all have alpha 255 (opaque vertex colours or material, the lighting's ambient alpha 255, and
a texture whose texels are all opaque or a DXT1 HD replacement), the test has one answer: when it passes, the draw
gets the program without it. GL_ALPHA_ELIDE=0 keeps every test.

Verified: about 400 of a mission frame's 640 draws qualify (376 with the 2x pack); 25 replayed gameplay frames are
pixel-identical with it on and off, with and without the HD pack, and so are four screenshots of a live mission-1
game; framework tests pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/docs/GL_RENDERER.md b/docs/GL_RENDERER.md
index 47cc136..dd27b8d 100644
--- a/docs/GL_RENDERER.md
+++ b/docs/GL_RENDERER.md
@@ -54,6 +54,12 @@ setting (the names are `gl_setting_names()` in `gl_renderer.hpp`), and `<PREFIX>
   light's shape (off, directional, point or spot; plain diffuse or not), which takes the Vita's vertex lighting
   program from about 600 instructions to 96–182. `GL_SPECIALIZE=0` (`--set specialize=0`) goes back to the
   uniform-driven programs; both give the same pictures.
+* **Alpha tests that decide nothing are dropped** (`GL_ALPHA_ELIDE`, on). Infected keeps the GE's alpha test on
+  ("greater than 0") for nearly everything. When every fragment of a draw has alpha 255 (opaque vertices or material,
+  and a texture whose texels are all opaque, or a DXT1 HD replacement), the comparison has one answer, so the draw
+  gets a program without the test and without `discard`, which on a tile-based GPU holds up the depth test of what
+  lies behind. About 400 of a mission frame's 640 draws qualify; the pictures are identical (replays with and without
+  the HD pack, and a live mission).
 * **Blending without `glBlendColor`.** `GL_CONSTANT_COLOR` factors are used only where the driver has them and
   the setting `no_blend_color` is off; otherwise the fragment shader pre-multiplies (`u_blend.x`: 1 doubles the
   source alpha, 2 doubles and complements, 3 multiplies by a fixed colour, 4 a fixed colour against its
diff --git a/host/gpu/gl/gl_hd_textures.cpp b/host/gpu/gl/gl_hd_textures.cpp
